# Route asip-api egress via mullvad-1

- **Timestamp:** 2026-07-29 ~08:45–08:50 UTC
- **Host:** t3-new (`ssh t3 -p 80`)
- **Stack:** `/home/cloud-admin/docker/asip`

## Changes

1. `docker-compose.yml` (`asip-api`):
   - Joined external network `openvpn-net` (DNS to `mullvad-1`)
   - Set `HTTP(S)_PROXY` / `http(s)_proxy` → `http://mullvad-1:8778` (3proxy sidecar `openrouter-proxy` in mullvad-1 netns)
   - Set `NO_PROXY` for `localhost,127.0.0.1,postgres,asip-postgres`
2. Recreated `asip-api` on server with updated compose

## Verify

```text
Networks: asip-net, openvpn-net, t3-net
Proxy env present on asip-api
curl --network container:asip-api -x http://mullvad-1:8778 https://am.i.mullvad.net/json
→ mullvad_exit_ip true, UK Manchester (gb-mnc-wg-003)
https://asip-api.xaigrok.ir/api/v1/health → 200 ok
```

## Result

Outbound internet from `asip-api` (git sync, HTTPS) goes through Mullvad via the shared `:8778` proxy. Inbound HAProxy path on `t3-net` and Postgres on `asip-net` unchanged.

## Warnings

- BusyBox `wget` in the image mishandles HTTPS-via-HTTP-proxy (400); `git`/`curl` work.
- Proxy depends on `mullvad-1` + `openrouter-proxy` staying up (`ensure-openrouter-proxy.sh`).
